WEBVTT

00:22.708 --> 00:26.041
ACROBATIC SHOW
FEMALE KNIFE THROWER

00:26.833 --> 00:27.708
Whoa!

00:29.166 --> 00:33.000
That's not what we wanna see!

00:33.083 --> 00:34.333
MANRAKU TROUPE

00:34.416 --> 00:36.208
That's some skill.

00:36.291 --> 00:40.083
Come on, no one cares
for knife-throwing at this day and age.

00:40.166 --> 00:42.958
With a pretty face like that,
why don't you just lose that kimono

00:43.041 --> 00:44.500
and sing us a song?

00:44.583 --> 00:47.125
-Damn right!
-Show us your beautiful fair skin!

00:47.208 --> 00:48.750
-Yeah!
-Pretty please!

00:52.958 --> 00:54.041
Oh wow.

00:54.125 --> 00:57.666
CIVILIZATION AND ENLIGHTENMENT

00:57.750 --> 00:59.458
Look at that!

00:59.541 --> 01:02.958
-Lose the kimono and do it again.
-Impressive. A lot of talent.

01:03.041 --> 01:04.083
I want one!

01:04.166 --> 01:05.458
-Me too.
-Come on then.

01:05.541 --> 01:07.541
-I can't keep doing this forever.
-I agree.

01:07.625 --> 01:09.916
-He was here.
-Can't we rest just this once?

01:10.000 --> 01:12.333
-I don't want to hear you complaining.
-I'm so stressed.

01:12.416 --> 01:13.541
-Creep.
-Iroha.

01:14.500 --> 01:18.166
Why not part with those blades
and start selling your body instead?

01:18.875 --> 01:21.041
I certainly wouldn't mind paying for it.

01:24.250 --> 01:25.375
What?

01:25.458 --> 01:28.500
What are you glaring at me for? Huh?

01:30.500 --> 01:32.875
You didn't forget
who took you in, did you?

01:33.458 --> 01:34.500
Hey.

01:40.000 --> 01:41.416
You're alive, huh?

01:43.041 --> 01:44.041
I'm glad.

01:44.833 --> 01:48.458
I never thought
you'd be a traveling performer.

01:48.541 --> 01:50.625
I could hardly recognize you.

01:50.708 --> 01:52.916
I'm surprised you didn't lose your temper.

01:53.000 --> 01:57.000
I bet the old Iroha would've put them
all in their graves.

01:57.083 --> 01:58.708
I'm already used to it.

01:59.708 --> 02:00.625
How have you been?

02:01.708 --> 02:03.041
Good.

02:03.125 --> 02:06.750
I've been out pulling a rickshaw
every day to feed my wife and daughter.

02:07.916 --> 02:10.791
I see. You have a family now, then.

02:10.875 --> 02:13.375
Yeah. What about you?

02:13.458 --> 02:15.666
What've you been doing
since you left the mountain?

02:18.458 --> 02:19.708
What I could.

02:20.416 --> 02:23.458
I traveled a lot,
always trying to hide from Gentosai.

02:25.666 --> 02:26.708
Hm.

02:27.458 --> 02:28.833
How's everybody?

02:43.708 --> 02:46.333
Fugoro and Shichiya
were killed by Gentosai.

02:48.791 --> 02:51.833
He's been searching
for the surviving disciples of our school.

02:54.291 --> 02:55.291
Iroha.

02:56.041 --> 02:58.458
If it goes on like this,
we'll definitely be killed too.

02:59.666 --> 03:02.250
I found Shikura and Jinroku
and talked them into it.

03:02.333 --> 03:03.750
They are joining me very soon.

03:06.083 --> 03:08.250
Joining you? What do you mean by that?

03:13.333 --> 03:16.416
We'll lure Gentosai into this
and finish him off ourselves.

03:16.500 --> 03:19.708
We'll never kill him
unless we strike together as siblings.

03:21.000 --> 03:22.000
Iroha.

03:24.750 --> 03:27.041
You know this is our fate as a family.

03:47.000 --> 03:49.083
Sorry for the wait.

03:50.125 --> 03:51.750
And now…

03:51.833 --> 03:54.000
…to uncover the true purpose
of this Kodoku,

03:54.083 --> 03:55.958
enters Kyojin, the great strategist--

03:56.041 --> 03:58.083
Can you just get to the point already?

04:00.958 --> 04:02.958
The plan has two parts.

04:03.041 --> 04:04.958
For the first experiment,

04:05.041 --> 04:08.416
we'll hand someone over to the authorities
with their tag still around their neck.

04:11.083 --> 04:13.541
They won't be able to make it
to Tokyo if they're incarcerated.

04:14.250 --> 04:15.916
It should count as a withdrawal.

04:16.000 --> 04:16.833
As of now,

04:16.916 --> 04:20.625
I still have no idea what they would do
to a contestant who's in jail.

04:20.708 --> 04:24.166
So you plan to find out if the rules
still count even in jail, right?

04:24.250 --> 04:25.083
Correct.

04:25.708 --> 04:29.083
Are they willing to go against the police
to silence a defeated contestant,

04:29.166 --> 04:32.250
or is that taking it a step too far,
even for those lunatics?

04:32.833 --> 04:35.916
This will show us how far the mastermind
is willing to take this Kodoku.

04:38.666 --> 04:40.333
For the second experiment,

04:41.000 --> 04:43.875
we'll figure out where all
of the dead bodies disappear to.

04:44.666 --> 04:46.125
-Disappear?
-Mm-hmm.

04:46.958 --> 04:49.208
With all these folks traveling
on the Tokaido Road,

04:49.291 --> 04:50.791
murdering each other left and right,

04:51.375 --> 04:55.666
it wouldn't be strange to see a dead body
or two along the way, and yet we don't.

04:55.750 --> 04:57.291
What does that tell you?

04:58.375 --> 05:00.791
That the bodies are taken
and hidden out of sight.

05:01.416 --> 05:03.000
Correct once again.

05:06.833 --> 05:08.666
By the way, they're always watching us.

05:08.750 --> 05:11.083
I'm sure you've all realized that
by now, haven't you?

05:14.166 --> 05:17.416
Well, they wouldn't follow us
inside this room, at least.

05:18.000 --> 05:20.291
But rest assured, they are watching us.

05:21.083 --> 05:24.833
So they're even cleaning up the corpses?
That's quite the undertaking, isn't it?

05:24.916 --> 05:28.375
Indeed. They're likely
hauling them off somewhere, hm?

05:28.458 --> 05:29.625
The conclusion here?

05:30.708 --> 05:32.250
They have concealed locations

05:32.333 --> 05:36.041
and the means to secretly haul hundreds
of dead bodies from all the towns.

05:36.125 --> 05:37.583
Splendid answer.

05:38.250 --> 05:40.333
If we find out
where the dead bodies are being hidden,

05:40.416 --> 05:43.041
we might figure out a little more
about the people behind this.

05:44.458 --> 05:47.125
What do you think?
It seems like a nice plan, right?

05:50.583 --> 05:53.833
Right. So where do we begin?

05:53.916 --> 05:57.708
First off, we go out there
and find our lucky volunteer.

06:30.500 --> 06:33.875
Why would the zaibatsu
purchase over 100 rifles

06:33.958 --> 06:36.375
and make the shizoku kill one another?

06:36.458 --> 06:37.833
Since the Meiji era began,

06:37.916 --> 06:40.333
they've likely been profiting
off government contracts.

06:41.833 --> 06:44.083
What on earth do they gain
from doing a thing like this?

06:45.958 --> 06:47.625
They're all betting, huh?

06:47.708 --> 06:50.083
Just so all those fools
will kill one another?

06:51.083 --> 06:53.750
Isn't there a chance
this is their actual purpose?

06:58.291 --> 07:01.125
Hatred for the former samurai?

07:01.208 --> 07:02.708
I'm sure it's no small burden,

07:02.791 --> 07:05.125
bearing the shizoku's
relentless plundering.

07:05.208 --> 07:07.541
There's one more thing I've learned.

07:07.625 --> 07:09.500
I checked with the zaibatsu,
and we've confirmed

07:09.583 --> 07:13.041
that these four individuals have been
on an extended leave since a week ago.

07:13.125 --> 07:16.416
No one knows where they went.
None of them were home.

07:17.541 --> 07:19.916
-Find them as soon as you can.
-Yes, sir.

07:20.416 --> 07:21.708
Lord Okubo.

07:21.791 --> 07:22.958
I mean no disrespect,

07:23.041 --> 07:25.916
but meddling with the zaibatsu
could bring repercussions to our economy.

07:26.000 --> 07:27.166
Mr. Nagase.

07:27.250 --> 07:29.291
If they are truly behind this,

07:29.375 --> 07:31.500
then this is treason against the state.

07:32.708 --> 07:35.333
We must deal with this
as soon as possible.

07:36.625 --> 07:37.958
-Kawaji.
-Sir.

07:38.041 --> 07:39.666
Bring the four of them here at once.

07:39.750 --> 07:42.291
Our efforts to find them
are already underway, sir.

07:43.958 --> 07:46.291
-I'll resume my work on the telegrams.
-Good.

07:57.500 --> 07:58.750
KUWANA-JUKU

07:58.833 --> 08:02.333
Have a look, have a taste!
Kuwana's famous grilled clams!

08:02.416 --> 08:04.541
Get yours while they're hot!

08:04.625 --> 08:09.583
We've got horse mackerel, squid,
clams and fine sake to wash it down!

08:10.125 --> 08:11.625
Been on the road a while, haven't you?

08:11.708 --> 08:13.791
How about a short break
before you carry on?

08:13.875 --> 08:15.458
Okay, right this way!

08:15.541 --> 08:18.583
Customers coming in!

08:18.666 --> 08:22.333
Welcome! A group of four coming in!

08:22.416 --> 08:23.708
Oh no!

08:24.958 --> 08:28.166
-Argh, I can't get it right.
-Shut up. You're distracting me.

08:31.250 --> 08:34.166
Come on in!
We have a table available in the back.

08:35.541 --> 08:37.291
We'll take some tea
and hotchpotch, please.

08:37.375 --> 08:38.333
Of course.

08:38.416 --> 08:40.500
Tea and four bowls of hotchpotch!

08:40.583 --> 08:41.500
All right!

08:44.166 --> 08:46.958
All right. One bowl of mixed rice

08:47.708 --> 08:49.916
and grilled squid, people.

08:55.791 --> 08:56.916
Look at that one.

08:57.916 --> 09:01.166
Didn't even bother to hide his tag.
That's quite some confidence.

09:05.208 --> 09:06.750
They're participants too.

09:06.833 --> 09:09.625
-Hey. Can't you see it's empty?
-I saw them at Tenryuji.

09:09.708 --> 09:11.375
-Hmm?
-I'm sorry. Let me do this.

09:11.458 --> 09:12.875
Who's our lucky volunteer?

09:12.958 --> 09:15.541
-What the hell is wrong with you?
-I'm sorry!

09:15.625 --> 09:17.625
You're a deadweight.
What the hell is your problem?

09:17.708 --> 09:19.916
-I'm really sorry! I'm sorry!
-Shut up!

09:20.875 --> 09:21.958
I'm sorry, sir.

09:22.041 --> 09:23.916
Let's go with
whoever leaves this teahouse first.

09:26.750 --> 09:29.583
That won't be necessary.

09:35.125 --> 09:36.291
Who the hell are you?

09:43.833 --> 09:46.083
More than one of you I guess, huh?

09:46.166 --> 09:47.125
"More than one?"

09:47.833 --> 09:50.916
Hmm… Yes, indeed. I would say we are.

09:53.333 --> 09:54.333
Hm?

09:56.458 --> 09:57.333
Oh.

10:04.208 --> 10:08.333
I figured most of the participants
would pass right by this teahouse,

10:08.416 --> 10:09.500
so I took the liberty

10:10.291 --> 10:12.416
of arranging
a delightful little trap here.

10:12.500 --> 10:16.000
I thought talking to outsiders was
a violation of the rules, right?

10:16.083 --> 10:18.833
But hiring them,
without revealing the details, is not.

10:18.916 --> 10:20.583
Aren't you the strategist?

10:20.666 --> 10:22.166
It's not too bad.

10:25.666 --> 10:27.458
As for the girls…

10:28.541 --> 10:31.666
Oh, you might as well
enjoy yourselves, boys.

10:40.208 --> 10:43.208
All right. I'll leave you to it.

10:54.875 --> 10:57.666
YOKKAICHI-SHUKU

11:07.500 --> 11:09.250
Lower-intermediate.

11:12.458 --> 11:13.750
Beginner.

11:16.583 --> 11:17.416
Hmm?

11:18.500 --> 11:20.166
Pre-intermediate.

11:38.916 --> 11:39.833
Hey.

11:41.125 --> 11:43.041
You're a contestant, aren't you?

11:43.125 --> 11:45.583
I'm looking for a swordsman
traveling with a girl.

11:45.666 --> 11:47.291
Have you seen anyone like that?

11:48.625 --> 11:49.625
No.

11:52.958 --> 11:56.208
How could I have let them slip
through my fingers the other night?

12:00.500 --> 12:01.625
A bow, huh?

12:01.708 --> 12:03.083
You're so far away.

12:03.166 --> 12:05.958
Where's the fun in killing someone
if you can't look 'em in the eye?

12:06.541 --> 12:08.791
No different from guns, is it?

12:10.833 --> 12:13.916
This is an instrument
for tributes and offerings to the gods.

12:14.500 --> 12:15.583
Nothing like a gun.

12:38.666 --> 12:40.875
To hell with all your gods.

12:41.625 --> 12:43.041
What nonsense.

12:44.041 --> 12:45.125
Darling!

12:45.708 --> 12:49.000
No! Stay with me, darling.

12:49.083 --> 12:52.708
Don't leave me like this, darling! No!

12:56.875 --> 12:59.375
If gods truly existed,

13:00.041 --> 13:02.958
do you think
this would be the state of the world?

13:20.166 --> 13:21.583
Huh. Nice.

13:26.041 --> 13:27.416
Let's have fun.

13:33.958 --> 13:36.125
He's coming! He's coming!

13:39.375 --> 13:41.083
Die, you rats!

13:41.166 --> 13:43.791
Oh.

13:44.291 --> 13:45.750
Go get the girls!

13:45.833 --> 13:46.750
Get them first!

13:46.833 --> 13:49.375
Get me their tags,
and I'll pay thrice the price!

14:20.750 --> 14:21.750
Outta the way!

14:25.208 --> 14:27.166
This trap isn't working out for you.

14:29.708 --> 14:32.833
Who are these people?
You told us this would be easy!

15:05.916 --> 15:08.416
Go! Hurry up! Go get them!

15:50.958 --> 15:52.833
Let go! Let go!

16:14.583 --> 16:16.875
Help! Someone warn the police!

16:51.708 --> 16:54.750
It's an offering for the gods, am I right?

17:10.625 --> 17:12.625
That's enough!

17:19.458 --> 17:21.375
Do I know you from somewhere?

17:21.458 --> 17:23.666
The police have been notified.
They're coming this way.

17:23.750 --> 17:26.208
Yeah, so what?

17:26.291 --> 17:29.208
The hosts have high expectations
of the two of you.

17:29.291 --> 17:31.291
Your failure would dull the thrill.

17:31.375 --> 17:33.291
You think I'll get caught?

17:34.416 --> 17:37.583
I could kill you right here and now.
Do you realize that?

17:38.250 --> 17:39.666
Suit yourself.

17:40.750 --> 17:43.375
If you think you can win
against this many rifles.

17:49.583 --> 17:51.333
This is no fun.

18:00.291 --> 18:02.125
The times have changed.

18:02.208 --> 18:04.583
The samurai have no place in this world.

18:06.125 --> 18:10.750
You suffered through the war,
and yet what came after was worse,

18:13.000 --> 18:15.125
Wasn't it, Kanjiya Bukotsu?

18:17.666 --> 18:20.375
Oh, my business is not your concern.

18:50.916 --> 18:53.458
All right. Which one of you, huh?

18:54.333 --> 18:55.750
Wait.

18:55.833 --> 18:58.208
What sort of scheme are you forcing on us?

18:58.291 --> 19:02.250
We'll hand one of you over to the police,
tag still round your neck.

19:02.833 --> 19:03.833
What?

19:05.125 --> 19:08.708
Uh, wait. I mean, if you do that--

19:08.791 --> 19:11.833
Either the Kodoku squad will kill you,
or the police will protect you.

19:11.916 --> 19:13.833
There's no telling which.

19:13.916 --> 19:14.958
What?

19:15.750 --> 19:17.333
What about the other one of us?

19:17.916 --> 19:20.333
We'll be taking their tag.
That's it, game over.

19:22.208 --> 19:24.791
Hand me over to the police!

19:25.833 --> 19:27.000
Please pick me to go!

19:27.083 --> 19:28.000
Huh?

19:28.083 --> 19:31.416
I'm doing it, not you.
Shut up and let me do it!

19:33.583 --> 19:36.166
Well, this is the end
of the line for you, I'm afraid.

19:40.083 --> 19:42.791
Please. I'll do anything.
Anything, please, I beg you!

19:42.875 --> 19:43.875
Just accept it.

19:43.958 --> 19:46.541
You've killed your share
of contestants yourself, haven't you?

19:46.625 --> 19:48.375
I've never killed anyone. I swear!

19:48.458 --> 19:51.541
Even at Tenryuji, I just stole the tags
from the men who died.

19:51.625 --> 19:54.500
-I'm not interested in your lies.
-I'm not lying!

19:56.083 --> 19:58.791
I was… threatened into it.

20:00.000 --> 20:02.041
He said I'd stay alive if I did this.

20:02.125 --> 20:03.875
Don't you lie!

20:07.125 --> 20:08.750
Our family's poor.

20:09.916 --> 20:12.500
I joined to help my father
with his business failures.

20:16.541 --> 20:18.125
I never imagined…

20:20.541 --> 20:22.375
we'd have to kill each other.

20:25.791 --> 20:27.583
But I simply cannot do it.

20:31.416 --> 20:32.750
I beg you not to kill me.

20:35.083 --> 20:36.208
Don't do it.

20:37.000 --> 20:38.791
Don't let it end like this, please!

20:45.625 --> 20:47.791
You think he's telling the truth?

20:55.750 --> 20:57.541
All right. You win.

20:59.500 --> 21:02.875
But in return,
you'll be at my side lending a hand.

21:06.833 --> 21:08.416
Thank you. Oh, thank you.

21:10.958 --> 21:12.458
Thank you very much!

21:13.416 --> 21:14.416
Huh?

21:15.125 --> 21:16.583
Hey, wait a minute.

21:16.666 --> 21:19.041
-Can I be at your side lending a ha--
-All right, Shujiro.

21:19.125 --> 21:21.000
You find out where
they're taking the bodies.

21:21.083 --> 21:22.375
All right.

21:22.458 --> 21:24.166
Oh, by the way, Iroha.

21:24.250 --> 21:25.833
Here you go.

21:27.791 --> 21:30.291
-What's this?
-It's a smoke ball.

21:30.375 --> 21:32.333
What am I going to do with this?

21:32.416 --> 21:33.833
Just keep it at hand.

21:34.333 --> 21:36.875
I'll have the police sent here.

21:36.958 --> 21:41.166
Take advantage of the ruckus to get past
the Kodoku guards keeping watch.

21:41.875 --> 21:42.958
Well… Ah!

21:44.000 --> 21:46.666
All right, let's go. The plan is launched.

21:54.000 --> 21:54.875
Come in.

21:58.750 --> 22:00.125
The analysis is complete.

22:00.208 --> 22:01.833
It's exactly as you suspected, sir.

22:02.416 --> 22:04.291
They rely on telegrams
for their communication.

22:04.375 --> 22:06.875
DOMESTIC TELEGRAM RECORD

22:06.958 --> 22:09.583
Since May 5th,
when we received reports from Tenryuji,

22:10.291 --> 22:12.208
there's been
a sudden increase in correspondence.

22:12.291 --> 22:14.041
NUMBER OF TELEGRAMS
MAY 5TH: 156

22:14.125 --> 22:15.375
Hmm.

22:15.458 --> 22:16.541
What else?

22:16.625 --> 22:18.583
We couldn't decipher the messages.

22:18.666 --> 22:20.416
They're using some sort of code.

22:25.333 --> 22:26.166
However,

22:26.750 --> 22:29.083
we managed to find out
where these telegrams originated.

22:30.291 --> 22:31.125
Go on.

22:31.708 --> 22:33.333
-Show him.
-Yes, sir.

22:39.875 --> 22:42.166
It's near the southern side of Mount Fuji.

22:43.750 --> 22:46.458
As you can see,
the map suggests there's nothing there.

22:46.541 --> 22:48.291
MOUNT FUJI
SHIZUOKA TELEGRAPH OFFICE

22:48.916 --> 22:51.500
That means their headquarters are there.

22:51.583 --> 22:53.083
Kawaji, head there now.

22:53.166 --> 22:54.291
Let us proceed.

23:04.250 --> 23:08.750
"Clash Between Shizoku
in Yokkaichi City on the Tokaido Road."

23:24.458 --> 23:25.500
Gentlemen.

23:26.416 --> 23:27.708
What is it?

23:27.791 --> 23:29.541
Looks like the state is taking action.

23:29.625 --> 23:30.458
What?

23:32.625 --> 23:34.708
Nothing to be worried about.

23:34.791 --> 23:38.208
They can't reach us here.
They couldn't possibly find us.

23:38.916 --> 23:43.166
Even if they did,
we're protected by a guardian god.

23:45.375 --> 23:49.041
Oh. That's right.
That's a fair point, my friend.

23:49.125 --> 23:51.375
Well said.

23:57.666 --> 24:00.375
Iroha-san.
Thank you for saving me earlier.

24:03.875 --> 24:07.458
I was wondering,
at what age did you start your training?

24:10.958 --> 24:14.000
All of us at Kyohachi-ryu
were abandoned as kids.

24:14.083 --> 24:15.750
We don't know our real ages.

24:16.333 --> 24:19.250
Were there other girls there?
Other than yourself?

24:20.875 --> 24:21.875
No.

24:23.541 --> 24:24.958
I was so young

24:26.541 --> 24:27.958
and the weakest of all.

24:28.541 --> 24:29.750
You were the weakest?

24:31.041 --> 24:32.750
It was a long time ago.

24:46.583 --> 24:48.916
I want to be as strong as you are.

24:49.000 --> 24:50.416
Can you share some advice?

24:59.583 --> 25:01.500
I wouldn't worry yourself with it.

25:02.458 --> 25:04.250
Strength won't help you win.

25:07.083 --> 25:09.416
No matter how skilled you become,

25:11.666 --> 25:13.791
happiness remains out of reach.

25:19.333 --> 25:20.958
He's here.

25:31.875 --> 25:34.000
Ow!

25:34.083 --> 25:38.416
Hey, that hurts. Hey.
Hey, a little gentleness, please! Argh!

25:39.166 --> 25:42.291
-Oh, sir.
-There was a murder at the teahouse.

25:42.375 --> 25:44.125
-He's the main suspect.
-No, no, no!

25:44.208 --> 25:45.791
We'll be holding him in jail.

25:45.875 --> 25:47.250
-Yes, sir.
-Let's go!

25:55.500 --> 25:58.125
Ah, I can't wait to see what happens next.

25:59.541 --> 26:01.041
-Please, don't!
-Shut up!

26:01.125 --> 26:02.500
POLICE BRANCH STATION

26:08.250 --> 26:10.875
You stay quiet in here.
We'll interrogate you later.

26:11.500 --> 26:12.583
Hey! Wait.

26:13.250 --> 26:15.833
Listen. Listen!

26:15.916 --> 26:17.208
Where's the guard?

26:19.416 --> 26:20.875
Shouldn't there be a guard here?

26:20.958 --> 26:24.333
What's wrong, huh?
Scared of spirits, are you?

26:24.416 --> 26:28.041
Oh, no way. Of course not.

26:28.625 --> 26:30.916
Oh hey! Wait! Wait! Hey! Don't!

26:31.500 --> 26:33.500
Hey! Don't leave me alone!

27:09.750 --> 27:10.916
Let's go.

27:25.833 --> 27:26.875
108

27:35.291 --> 27:38.500
Police Bureau.
The chief knows we're coming.

27:38.583 --> 27:39.500
Oh.

27:42.125 --> 27:43.958
Looks like our bait worked, huh?

27:44.541 --> 27:46.333
-Huh?
-What's your name, kiddo?

27:47.750 --> 27:49.708
Uh, Sayama Shinnosuke, sir.

27:49.791 --> 27:51.875
Shinnosuke, hold these for me.

27:51.958 --> 27:53.041
Huh?

27:53.625 --> 27:54.708
Uh, wait.

28:00.416 --> 28:04.333
Seventeen past two, 108, Saga Shujiro.

28:22.916 --> 28:25.333
We're here to interrogate the suspect
who was just detained.

28:25.416 --> 28:28.000
Yes, sir. Uh, he's in the basement.

28:28.083 --> 28:29.750
I'll show you the way. Ah.

28:37.375 --> 28:38.500
Hello, sir.

28:43.500 --> 28:44.416
Hello.

28:45.458 --> 28:47.458
I'll join them for the interrogation.

28:47.541 --> 28:48.541
Yes, sir.

29:44.333 --> 29:45.833
Wait a second, this is…

30:10.083 --> 30:14.166
108, Saga Shujiro was eliminated
at 2:17 p.m. in Kuwana.

32:02.000 --> 32:05.625
MITSUI BANK
RECORD OF ALL TRANSACTIONS

32:05.708 --> 32:07.708
MITSUI BANK OPENING LOAN DEPOSIT

32:08.375 --> 32:10.208
MITSUI BANK GUIDELINES
FOR ESTIMATING WRITE-OFFS

32:10.291 --> 32:12.041
MITSUI BANK
INTERNAL RULES

32:19.166 --> 32:20.458
Wait, is this…

32:29.791 --> 32:31.083
MITSUI BANK

32:31.166 --> 32:32.333
A bank.

32:41.750 --> 32:43.250
I know that man.

33:12.125 --> 33:13.625
Here to question me?

33:15.000 --> 33:16.000
Listen to me.

33:16.916 --> 33:20.583
I didn't kill anyone, all right?
It's complex, but I can explain.

33:21.166 --> 33:23.958
Some unknown devils
are making us slaughter each other.

33:24.041 --> 33:26.208
They're killing whoever tries to escape.

33:26.291 --> 33:28.708
I need someone to guard me down here.

33:29.291 --> 33:32.708
Please! Keep those madmen away from me.

33:40.250 --> 33:41.625
Wait.

33:41.708 --> 33:42.750
Wait, no! Wait, wait!

34:51.041 --> 34:53.666
-So 108's body is here?
-Yes, sir.

35:28.583 --> 35:31.541
It seems like
a mouse has made its way inside.

35:43.458 --> 35:44.916
And who might you be?

35:49.708 --> 35:51.708
Fourth Division. The name's Takayama.

35:54.958 --> 35:58.041
I don't remember any
of my subordinates going by that name.

35:59.250 --> 36:02.166
Oh, so you're Fourth Division too.

36:02.666 --> 36:03.500
Mm.

36:04.375 --> 36:06.125
Best answer you could find…

36:09.041 --> 36:10.375
…Tsuge Kyojin?

36:47.500 --> 36:49.708
You forgot to plan an escape route, huh?

36:51.541 --> 36:52.583
Come out.

36:53.875 --> 36:56.208
No use dragging this out any longer…

37:01.041 --> 37:02.583
Saga Kokushu.

37:17.041 --> 37:18.500
Nakamura Hanjiro.

37:19.541 --> 37:21.833
I go by the name of Sakura now.

37:22.500 --> 37:25.416
When I saw you kill Ando
at Tenryuji Temple,

37:25.500 --> 37:27.125
I had my suspicions.

37:27.208 --> 37:30.083
I have been secretly rooting for you.

37:30.166 --> 37:32.000
Back then, I was sure you were dead.

37:38.750 --> 37:40.541
Strange how that works.

37:41.125 --> 37:43.083
Life is surprising.

37:45.333 --> 37:47.500
For as long as I can remember,

37:48.458 --> 37:50.958
I wanted to be just like you, you know.

37:52.333 --> 37:54.125
Just tell me one thing.

37:56.375 --> 37:58.625
What are you all hoping to achieve?

38:01.041 --> 38:02.916
I cannot answer that, I'm afraid.

38:06.166 --> 38:08.416
But when old comrades reunite,

38:08.500 --> 38:10.708
they either drink together…

38:13.500 --> 38:14.750
or they fight.

38:17.500 --> 38:19.375
It's one or the other.

39:31.458 --> 39:32.833
Our analysis, sir.

39:32.916 --> 39:36.333
All of the coded telegrams were sent
to or from this location,

39:36.416 --> 39:38.916
the Nihonbashi Telegraph Office.

39:39.000 --> 39:40.291
From there,

39:40.375 --> 39:42.541
we managed to track down
the recipient of the telegrams

39:42.625 --> 39:44.250
and pinpoint their location.

39:45.625 --> 39:47.541
It's not what we expected.

39:49.458 --> 39:50.666
What is it?

39:51.791 --> 39:54.291
The final destination
of these telegrams was…

39:57.000 --> 39:59.375
the Police Bureau, our own.

40:15.375 --> 40:18.666
Gentlemen. Sorry to keep you waiting.

40:19.250 --> 40:20.708
We're glad you're here, sir.

40:21.750 --> 40:25.000
I'm sure you were very busy
from overseeing all this, right?

40:25.083 --> 40:26.583
Mmm.

40:47.166 --> 40:48.291
Lord Okubo,

40:49.166 --> 40:52.000
I don't mean
to speak out of turn, but I must ask…

40:56.000 --> 40:57.083
Go ahead.

40:59.458 --> 41:01.791
Are you certain that we can trust Kawaji?

41:09.500 --> 41:14.166
Once again, thank you all for being here
and for your continued support.

41:16.375 --> 41:18.791
It's all for the good of this country.

41:18.875 --> 41:22.666
-Whatever you need, don't hesitate to ask.
-Thank you very much.

41:26.708 --> 41:28.291
This is a critical endeavor.

41:28.375 --> 41:30.375
The samurai are like ghosts,

41:31.250 --> 41:33.208
and we must eradicate them at all costs.

41:35.583 --> 41:37.083
So, gentlemen,

41:37.166 --> 41:39.791
let's see this mission through together…

41:57.708 --> 42:00.958
…for the sake of our country's tomorrow.

42:21.916 --> 42:26.208
70 REMAINING
